Conclusion:
The exploratory data analysis of the sales dataset provides useful insights into the distribution and characteristics of the data. The mean and median values help understand the central tendency, while the standard deviation indicates the variability present in the numerical features. Histograms show the distribution pattern of numerical variables, helping identify skewness and spread. Box plots highlight the presence of outliers and give a clear summary of data dispersion. Bar charts for categorical variables reveal the frequency distribution of different categories. Overall, the dataset contains a mix of numerical and categorical features with some variations and possible outliers, which should be considered for further analysis or model building.